# tests/adapt/lint.allow: hardware constants the lint accepts (docs/uni/principles.md, rule 1).
# PATH<TAB>REGEX<TAB>reason. A hit in PATH whose line matches REGEX passes. Entries marked U2
# are upstream code that milestone U2 makes vendor-neutral; the others are where a constant
# belongs (test data, a file a hwdb rule selects, a runtime rule that names its driver).
install/00-probe.sh	.	U2: upstream's human report (MSI's EC, the AX201's Bluetooth); its machine knowledge moves to hwdb notes
rootfs/etc/udev/rules.d/99-vh-dgpu-off.rules	.	installed only when hwdb's gpu.nvidia.dgpu-off selects it (VH_PLAN_UDEV)
rootfs/etc/udev/rules.d/99-vh-net.rules	RTL81	a runtime rule by driver (r8169), a no-op on every other machine; the comment names the chips
kernel/src/hw.zig	GF63|Micro-Star|usb:v8087	test data: the GF63 fixture
kernel/src/probe.zig	GF63|Micro-Star|MS-16R5|usb:v8087	test data: the GF63 fixture
kernel/src/resolve.zig	GF63	test data: the GF63 fixture
adapt/src/facts.zig	pci:v00008086|usb:v8087	test data: modalias examples
adapt/src/tests.zig	.	unit tests on a machine written in the test
kernel/profiles/features/game	DRM_NOUVEAU	track G (upstream): the gaming feature is built around the NVIDIA open modules; vendor-neutral gaming is a U-milestone of track G
